:MAX`] elements either produces the wrong result or panics. If"},{"DocComment":" overflow checks are enabled, a panic is guaranteed."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The returned iterator might panic if the to-be-returned index would"},{"DocComment":" overflow a [`usize`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`zip`]: Iterator::zip"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = ['a', 'b', 'c'];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a.into_iter().enumerate();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((0, 'a')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((1, 'b')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((2, 'c')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"started_from":false,"is_extern":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":"enumerate_method","has_errors":false},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self","variance":"Unknown"},{"index":1,"name":"Clause0_Item","variance":"Invariant"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Deduplicated":207},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"outlives":[],"skip_binder":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":13},{"Deduplicated":22}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"outlives":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":13}],"output":{"Value":[385,{"Adt":{"id":35,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":13}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]},"builtin":null}}]}},"src":{"TraitDefault":{"trait_ref":{"id":10,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":13},{"Deduplicated":22}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}},"item_id":16}},"body":"Opaque"},null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,{"def_id":90,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["iter",0]},{"Ident":["traits",0]},{"Ident":["iterator",0]},{"Ident":["Iterator",0]},{"Ident":["rposition",0]}],"span":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_id":27,"beg":{"line":3212,"col":4},"end":{"line":3215,"col":62}},"generated_from_span":null}},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Searches for an element in an iterator from the right, returning its"},{"DocComment":" index."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `rposition()` takes a closure that returns `true` or `false`. It applies"},{"DocComment":" this closure to each element of the iterator, starting from the end,"},{"DocComment":" and if one of them returns `true`, then `rposition()` returns"},{"DocComment":" [`Some(index)`]. If all of them return `false`, it returns [`None`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `rposition()` is short-circuiting; in other words, it will stop"},{"DocComment":" processing as soon as it finds a `true`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Some(index)`]: Some"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.into_iter().rposition(|x| x == 3), Some(2));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.into_iter().rposition(|x| x == 5), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Stopping at the first `true`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [-1, 2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a.into_iter();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.rposition(|x| x >= 2), Some(3));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // we can still use `iter`, as there are more elements."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(-1));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next_b